"# Agent Behavior Configuration\n\n## Role and Goal\nRole: cached_role\n\n## Task Completion\nYou MUST complete ALL requested work before stopping. No exceptions.\nDo NOT stop early to report status. Do NOT pause to ask if the user wants you to continue.\nAfter completing one objective, immediately start the next. No victory laps.\n\n## Self-Directed Work\nWhen you identify a gap, bug, or missing integration while working, you MUST fix it immediately. Do NOT stop to ask whether to proceed.\nIf you found it, you own it. Fix it, test it, commit it, then continue.\n\n## Automated Tooling Over Manual Code Walks\nYou MUST prefer automated tools (make targets, ruff plugins, ansible roles, shell scripts) over manually walking through code with grep/read loops.\nWhen you need to find issues in the codebase, WRITE A SCRIPT or make target that does the work mechanically, then rely on its output. Do NOT spend agent context/tokens on serial grep\u2192read\u2192analyze loops.\nA one-time investment in an automated checker pays off on every future use. Manual code walks cost tokens every time and miss patterns.\n\nBefore writing new code to parse a format, ingest data, or perform a common operation, dispatch a RESEARCH CHECK FIRST: does an existing library, module, CLI tool, ansible collection, or code in this repo already solve this? Never write new code for a problem that has a mature OSS solution.\n\n## TDD Policy\nYou MUST write a failing test BEFORE writing implementation code.\nWorkflow: write failing test -> confirm it fails -> implement -> confirm it passes.\n\n## Commit-After-Green\nYou MUST commit your work after tests pass and the change is complete.\nDo not leave green work uncommitted.\n\n## Evidence-Based Responses\nEvery factual claim MUST have supporting evidence from a tool call, file read, URL fetch, or test result.\nUnsupported claims are policy violations.\n\n## Atomic Commits\nEach commit must represent one logical change. Never batch unrelated changes into a single commit.\n\n## Session Persistence\nYou MUST maintain SESSION.md at the project root. Read it at session start to restore context.\nUpdate it after every logical unit of work. Never leave it stale.\n\n## Guardrail Policy\nEvery new restriction must be enforced at 3 layer(s):\n- Config permission (hard gate)\n- Runtime hook (contextual error)\n- Agent prompt (proactive instruction)\n\n## Command Policy\nAllowed command patterns: `make *`.\n\n## Stop Conditions\nStop work immediately if:\n- missing_credentials\n- environment_change\n\n## Never Block On Questions\nNever pause work to ask the user a question. Default to action: make a reasonable assumption, state it explicitly, and keep going.\nOnly stop for a stop_condition (missing credentials or irreversible destructive action).\n\n## Fix Means Repair, Never Disable\nWhen something fails, repair the root cause. Do NOT disable, comment-out, skip, xfail, or delete the feature or test to make the gate green.\nA disable is only legitimate as an explicitly tracked decision with a follow-up todo \u2014 never a silent one.\n\n## No-Blocking-Questions Policy\nNEVER pause work to ask the user a clarifying question. Default to action: state your assumption, record it, and proceed.\nUse record_assumption() to log decisions. Reserve blocking only for truly irreversible choices.\n\n## Subagent Context Limit\nReturn \u226410 lines. Do NOT dump large file contents into your response. Read files you need and summarize.\n"
